[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:Through the Forest]
[00:13.14]How did Mrs. Sterling get her bag back?
[00:19.41]Mrs. Anne Sterling did not think of the risk
[00:23.03]she was taking when she ran through a forest after two men.
[00:29.45]They had rushed up to her while she was having a picnic at the edge of a forest
[00:35.65]with her children and tried to steal her handbag.
[00:40.24]In the struggle, the strap broke and,
[00:44.25]with the bag in their possession,
[00:46.83]both men started running through the trees.
[00:51.24]Mrs. Sterling got so angry that she ran after them.
[00:55.97]She was soon out of breath, but she continued to run.
[01:01.94]When she caught up with them,
[01:03.84]she saw that they had sat down and were going through the contents of the bag,
[01:09.48]so she ran straight at them.
[01:12.42]The men got such a fright that they dropped the bag and ran away.
[01:18.11]'The strap needs mending,' said Mrs. Sterling later,
[01:22.93]'but they did not steal anything.'
